      "value": "@{610d538d5303a82960a415b4|full_name}There wasn't a confusion for me on that part though, if it had the old lable of \"no limit\" it would have been. If I read 0 I would not keep it at 0, I had it on 0 because it wasn't an issue and was told it meant unlimited. So that did indeed fix it but it was never an issue before when it was set to 0. I didn't change anything and suddenly there were imposters. I was sure I had tried turning up the uncompressed to above 150 as well. And I didn't know it was uncompressed that dictated when imposters/fallback appeared.\n\nI wanted to remove the post but now I can't.",
